senv does not copy OpenEnv source. The Python compatibility tests import the
unmodified EchoEnv and TextArenaEnv clients from a checkout of that commit.

Wordle-v0 rules (5 letters, 6 guesses, green-before-yellow marking, one free
invalid move) were reimplemented from the public behavior of TextArena's
Wordle environment and from OpenEnv's TextArenaEnv client. senv does not copy
that source. The bundled word list is not TextArena's list and not the New
York Times word list.

The session kernel executes on h5i-app from https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i
at commit 5e0f8a929c57bb12a321090d98a14b3a2714b849, which is licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.
